<title>SWEDEN: Cancer drug firm Oxigene debuts in Sweden.</title>
<headline>Cancer drug firm Oxigene debuts in Sweden.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1996-11-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish drugs company Oxigene made its debut on the Stockholm bourse's O-list on Tuesday, trading at 175 crowns.</p>
<p>This was an increase of 8.50 crowns compared to its issue price of 166.50 crowns for one million shares. The issue was designed to raise 191.5 million crowns.</p>
<p>Trade was relatively light with 2,800 shares traded at 0935 gmt.</p>
<p>Oxigene is conducting clinical studies on drugs to treat cancer.</p>
<p>These drugs include Neu-Sensamide which is being developed to use as a radio-sensitiser in all cancers treated with radiotherapy.</p>
<p>-- Belinda Goldsmith, Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700-1045</p>
